From: Marek Czernohous <marek@czernohous.de>
Date: 2026-08-06
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau: subscribe to the channel-kill event after the fence context

Lokale Entsprechung zu v3 2/5 der ML-Serie, angepasst an den hier
laufenden Stack (das Abo-Gate traegt durch 0019 den Modulparameter
chan_kill_event).

nouveau_channel_init() schaltet das Kill-Abo scharf, bevor der
Fence-Kontext existiert. Die Backends setzen chan->fence per kzalloc,
bevor nouveau_fence_context_new() spin_lock_init(&fctx->lock) und
INIT_LIST_HEAD(&fctx->pending) ausfuehrt. Der Guard if (chan->fence) in
nouveau_channel_kill() greift in diesem Fenster nicht: der Zeiger ist
non-NULL und unbrauchbar, nouveau_fence_context_kill() nimmt ein nie
initialisiertes Spinlock und laeuft ueber einen Listenkopf, dessen next
noch die NULL von kzalloc traegt.

Auf Tesla ist das erst erreichbar, seit 0019 das Abo auf NV50 gesenkt hat
und 0020 einen Kanal-Killer mitbringt. Gefunden vom Sashiko-Review-Bot
auf der v2-Einreichung vom 2026-08-06.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Marek Czernohous <marek@czernohous.de>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_chan.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_chan.c
@@ -366,34 +366,6 @@ nouveau_channel_init(struct nouveau_chan
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* Patch 0020a: subscribe channel-killed events on NV50+ (Tesla) too, not
-	 * only Fermi+.  Without a subscriber the nvkm ERRORED event (fifo/chan.c)
-	 * is a dead letter, nouveau_fence_context_kill() never runs, and the
-	 * killed channel's fences never signal: display commits (disp.c) and TTM
-	 * then wait forever (dma-fence contract violation).  Runtime escape:
-	 * nouveau.chan_kill_event=0 restores the legacy Fermi+-only behaviour. */
-	if (chan->user.oclass >= (nouveau_chan_kill_event ?
-				  NV50_CHANNEL_GPFIFO : FERMI_CHANNEL_GPFIFO)) {
-		DEFINE_RAW_FLEX(struct nvif_event_v0, args, data,
-				sizeof(struct nvif_chan_event_v0));
-		struct nvif_chan_event_v0 *host =
-				(struct nvif_chan_event_v0 *)args->data;
-
-		host->version = 0;
-		host->type = NVIF_CHAN_EVENT_V0_KILLED;
-
-		ret = nvif_event_ctor(&chan->user, "abi16ChanKilled", chan->chid,
-				      nouveau_channel_killed, false,
-				      args, __struct_size(args), &chan->kill);
-		if (ret == 0)
-			ret = nvif_event_allow(&chan->kill);
-		if (ret) {
-			NV_ERROR(drm, "Failed to request channel kill "
-				      "notification: %d\n", ret);
-			return ret;
-		}
-	}
-
 	/* allocate dma objects to cover all allowed vram, and gart */
 	if (device->info.family < NV_DEVICE_INFO_V0_FERMI) {
 		if (device->info.family >= NV_DEVICE_INFO_V0_TESLA) {
@@ -497,7 +469,46 @@ nouveau_channel_init(struct nouveau_chan
 	}
 
 	/* initialise synchronisation */
-	return nouveau_fence(drm)->context_new(chan);
+	ret = nouveau_fence(drm)->context_new(chan);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Subscribe to the channel-kill event last: the handler dereferences
+	 * chan->fence, and the backends publish that pointer from kzalloc()
+	 * before nouveau_fence_context_new() initialises the lock and the
+	 * pending list.  An event in between would find a non-NULL but
+	 * unusable context.  Upstream as v3 2/5.
+	 */
+	/* Patch 0020a: subscribe channel-killed events on NV50+ (Tesla) too, not
+	 * only Fermi+.  Without a subscriber the nvkm ERRORED event (fifo/chan.c)
+	 * is a dead letter, nouveau_fence_context_kill() never runs, and the
+	 * killed channel's fences never signal: display commits (disp.c) and TTM
+	 * then wait forever (dma-fence contract violation).  Runtime escape:
+	 * nouveau.chan_kill_event=0 restores the legacy Fermi+-only behaviour. */
+	if (chan->user.oclass >= (nouveau_chan_kill_event ?
+				  NV50_CHANNEL_GPFIFO : FERMI_CHANNEL_GPFIFO)) {
+		DEFINE_RAW_FLEX(struct nvif_event_v0, args, data,
+				sizeof(struct nvif_chan_event_v0));
+		struct nvif_chan_event_v0 *host =
+				(struct nvif_chan_event_v0 *)args->data;
+
+		host->version = 0;
+		host->type = NVIF_CHAN_EVENT_V0_KILLED;
+
+		ret = nvif_event_ctor(&chan->user, "abi16ChanKilled", chan->chid,
+				      nouveau_channel_killed, false,
+				      args, __struct_size(args), &chan->kill);
+		if (ret == 0)
+			ret = nvif_event_allow(&chan->kill);
+		if (ret) {
+			NV_ERROR(drm, "Failed to request channel kill "
+				      "notification: %d\n", ret);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 int
